R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10002 - Users & Accounts
Preferences now includes Users & Accounts. It lists the accounts that already exist on this computer (name, user id, home folder, and whether the account looks like an administrator). You cannot yet add people, set passwords, log in as someone else, or keep separate desktops. Everyone still shares the same session.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - IPv6
On a home network the computer can take an IPv6 address from the router as well as IPv4, and use that address to reach the rest of the network. Open Network, select the card, and look under IPv6. Automatic is the default. You should see a link-local address and, if the router offers one, a second address. Set IPv6 to Disabled if you do not want that.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - Shutdown
Shutting down should no longer sit forever while IPv6 autoconfig (SLAAC) is still listening. If it still hangs, say so — ACPI power-off is a different path.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - AirPlay
We've added AirPlay so you can play this computer's sound on speakers on your Wi-Fi network, such as Sonos. Open the AirPlay icon in the Deskbar, pick a speaker, and choose Play to. You can also receive classic AirPlay 1 audio on this computer. An iPhone usually will not list R5OS in Control Center yet — AirPlay 2 pairing is not included.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - Wi-Fi
Wi-Fi is on one screen: scan, enter a password, and connect. Open it from Network preferences or from the network icon in the Deskbar. Networks you join are remembered, and R5OS can reconnect after sleep or a dropped link. The Deskbar tooltip shows the network name, or that it is still connecting.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - AirPrint
You can add network printers that speak AirPrint or IPP. Open the printer settings, add a printer, and choose one that appears on the network. This is new; not every printer has been tried.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - Dark Mode
You can switch the desktop to a dark look. Open Preferences → Appearance, choose a dark color scheme, and apply it. More of the system (Deskbar, Tracker, windows) follows those colors than before. Some apps still keep their own look.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - Desktop and Deskbar
Icons on the Desktop overlap less, sit clearer of the Deskbar, and keep a sensible size. The Deskbar clock, mute, battery, and menus behave more predictably. Lists, scrollbars, and alert windows clip and resize more cleanly.

R5OS 2026.1-dev Build 10001 - Name and About
The system identifies as R5OS in the Deskbar, installer, boot splash, and About R5OS. Open About R5OS from the Deskbar leaf menu. This is not an official Haiku release.
